1. Business Model Overview

RTCM Platform LLC operates as a cloud-native Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) business. Revenue is generated through recurring annual and monthly subscription contracts, priced by the number of legal entities monitored and the feature tier selected. There are no per-user fees — pricing is entity-based, reflecting how mid-market finance teams actually operate: a single Controller or CFO is responsible for multiple entities simultaneously.
RTCM's cost structure is favorable for scale: the core control evaluation engine, database infrastructure, and ERP connectors are built once and serve unlimited clients. Marginal cost per additional client is low, creating strong operating leverage as the customer base grows.

2. Target Market

RTCM is purpose-built for three primary customer segments:

2.1 Private Equity-Backed Portfolio Companies
Private equity firms managing three or more portfolio companies face a systemic challenge: each portfolio company has its own ERP, its own finance team, and its own control environment — but the PE sponsor has no real-time visibility into control health across the portfolio. RTCM solves this at both the portfolio company level (entity-level monitoring) and the portfolio level (consolidated dashboard across all entities).
Estimated addressable market: Approximately 8,000 PE-backed U.S. companies with $10M–$500M in revenue (PitchBook, 2024).

2.2 Mid-Market Private Companies Preparing for Audit or Transaction
Companies preparing for their first external audit, a strategic sale, or an initial public offering need to demonstrate internal control maturity. RTCM compresses the timeline for achieving audit-ready control documentation from 12–18 months of manual effort to continuous, automated monitoring.
Estimated addressable market: Approximately 180,000 U.S. companies with $10M–$500M in revenue (U.S. Census Bureau, Statistics of U.S. Businesses, 2022).

2.3 CPA Firms and Outsourced CFO Providers

Regional CPA firms and fractional CFO service providers serve hundreds of mid-market clients each. RTCM's white-label partner program enables these firms to deliver automated control monitoring as a managed service — creating a recurring revenue stream for the firm while dramatically expanding RTCM's distribution without a proportional increase in sales cost.
Estimated addressable market: Approximately 44,000 U.S. CPA firms with at least one mid-market client (AICPA, 2023).

3. Pricing Model

RTCM pricing is structured around three subscription tiers, each priced per legal entity per month:

Tier 1 — Starter
Target: Single-entity companies or small multi-entity organizations (1–3 entities)
Price: $499 per entity per month (billed annually) / $599 month-to-month
Includes:
GL monitoring (15 controls)
Reconciliation tracking
Basic alert dashboard
QuickBooks Online connector
Email alert notifications
Up to 5-10 users

Tier 2 — Professional
Target: Mid-market multi-entity organizations (4–15 entities)
Price: $349 per entity per month (billed annually) / $419 month-to-month
Includes everything in Starter, plus:

Full control library (40+ controls)
Segregation of Duties analyzer
Intercompany monitor
NetSuite and Sage Intacct connectors
Webhook integrations
Audit export package
Unlimited users

Tier 3 — Enterprise
Target: PE portfolio platforms, large multi-entity consolidators (16+ entities)
Price: Custom — annual contract, negotiated based on entity count and feature scope
Includes everything in Professional, plus:
ML-powered anomaly detection
Narrative Intelligence module (AI-assisted control documentation)
CPA firm white-label option
Dedicated implementation support
SLA with uptime guarantee
SOC 2 Type II audit report access

Partner Program (CPA Firms)

CPA firm partners receive a 30% revenue share on all clients referred and managed through the partner portal. Partners receive access to a white-labeled version of the platform branded under their firm name, with RTCM branding removed from client-facing materials.

