5. Go-to-Market Strategy

Phase 1 — Direct Outreach (Q4 2026)
During the development phase, Mr. Santillo will leverage his professional network — Deloitte alumni, PE operating partners, UFT network contacts, and CPA firm relationships — to identify 2–3 pilot clients willing to participate in a no-cost pilot program in exchange for structured product feedback.
Target pilot profile: PE-backed company with 4–12 entities on QuickBooks or NetSuite, with an existing Controller or Director of Accounting who can serve as internal champion.

Phase 2 — CPA Firm Channel (Q1–Q2 2027)
CPA firms represent the most capital-efficient distribution channel for RTCM. A single regional firm serving 30 mid-market clients can deliver 30 potential RTCM subscribers through one partnership agreement. The partner program will be launched alongside general availability, targeting 2 initial firm partners in Q1 2027 and expanding to 10 by Q4 2027.
Phase 3 — Direct Digital and Content (Q2 2027 onward)
The rtcmplatform.com waitlist and demo request infrastructure will be supported by a content marketing program targeting finance leaders at PE-backed organizations: blog posts, LinkedIn content, and contributed articles in publications such as Accounting Today, CFO Magazine, and Private Equity Wire addressing the mid-market internal control gap.
Phase 4 — PE Sponsor Relationships (Q3 2027 onward)
The highest-leverage distribution path is a relationship with a private equity sponsor: a single PE firm with 10+ portfolio companies becomes a potential RTCM enterprise contract covering all portfolio entities. Mr. Santillo's existing relationships in the PE-backed company ecosystem position RTCM to pursue these relationships as the product matures.

